# No browser testing

Do not open the app or use browser tools to check your work. This includes navigation, clicks, typing, screenshots, and DevTools.

This overrides any general instruction to verify UI in the browser before finishing.

- Implement the change, then stop.
- For UI, layout, styling, routing, client state, or rendered data, tell the user what changed and what to look at. Ask them to check it and request corrections.
- Do not declare that UI work verified, and do not keep iterating from what you see in a browser.
- Checks that do not use a browser (unit tests, API calls, logs) are still fine when they fit the task.
